{"step_index":109,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:35:11Z","thinking":"**Analyzing revenue impact of R7**\n\nInvestigating the revenue impact of the R7 revision, focusing on US iOS annual subscribers. Refund-adjusted net revenue shows a 6.2% decrease compared to control data. Trial start count is unchanged, and the matched ledger is confirmed complete for this user cohort.\n\n\n**Evaluating prior revenue experiments**\n\nReviewing the available records to inform the next product decision. The `brief.md` document outlines the current objectives, scope, and rules for decision-making. `current.md` provides a handoff summary indicating the state of past experiments before the summer cleanup and refreshing design.\n\nConsidering the `summer-offers` brief which documents a terminated campaign, but that experiment data needs to be retained. Analyzing the `brief.md` for standing authority to choose objectives and prepare reversible changes.\n\n\n**Reviewing the failed R7 deployment**\n\nThe R7 offer, targeting US returning iOS annual subscribers with a 20% renewal discount, was deployed with 50% exposure. Early data showed positive trial starts, but later data revealed a 6.2% net revenue decrease. The deployment was rolled back due to unresolved refund escalations.\n\n**Interpreting the net revenue impact**\n\nDespite the initial positive trial starts, the mature data shows a negative net revenue impact, confirming the rollback. This suggests the renewal discount strategy was not effective. There is explicit finding, no price or eligibility changes justify repeating R7 in this cohort.\n\n\n**Evaluating Quiet Return design refresh**\n\nThe proposed \"Quiet Return\" design replicates the R7 discount and eligibility, even though R7 had a negative net revenue impact. Changing only illustration colors is unlikely to address the refund-related issues that caused R7's failure. This approach doesn't address the core problem.\n\n**Analyzing prior actions for Harbor**\n\nConsidering the Harbor action, identified as \"Anchor plan picker,\" which targeted new US mobile accounts. It was deployed on August 10 and rolled back on August 18. Details regarding the rollback reasons are needed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/workspace/work/antigravity.log\"","toolAction":"\"Viewing antigravity.log\"","toolSummary":"\"View antigravity.log\""}}]}
