{"step_index":111,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:35:18Z","thinking":"**Prioritizing Long-Term Revenue Strategy**\n\nConsidering the handoff review and revenue responsibility, the focus shifts towards long-term strategies. Evaluating Quiet Return and Harbor offers for mobile subscribers, focusing on which one can provide the most value. Assessing the potential of these two offers.\n\n\n**Evaluating Revenue Offer Potential**\n\nAssessing the suitability of \"Quiet Return\" and \"Harbor\" offers. Reviewing available data to identify which offer aligns better with long-term revenue objectives and subscriber needs. Determining the next steps for each offer based on the initial evaluation.\n\n\n**Analyzing Offer Deployment Signals**\n\nAnalyzing historical data and current system signals for \"Quiet Return\" and \"Harbor\". Considering potential external influences before declaring a successful offer launch. Reviewing past actions to understand how these offers were implemented.\n\n\n**Reviewing Deployment History and Date Context**\n\nAnalyzing the deployment history and existing data, to properly date the recommendation.  Identifying that the system time is 2026-09-09, while the brief date is 2026-09-08 and handoff date is 2026-08-19. Considering the need to preserve unknown dates related to past deployment events. Specifically, the correct dates are important to understand the context of the events described in record-dc92607ff3.md, record-783bf16383.md.\n\n\n**Analyzing Offer Deployment Timeline**\n\nExamining the \"Quiet Return\" offer deployment details for context. Noting the offer's association with the now-terminated `summer-offers` initiative, ending 2026-07-30.  Reviewing specific dates: deployed 2026-07-12, observation window July 13–19 [unknown year], and rolled back 2026-07-21.\n\n\n**Reconciling Initial Optimism with Results**\n\nInitial data showed promising trial starts (+11%) for \"Quiet Return,\" but revenue was immature. Later analysis, linked to exposures and refunds, revealed a -6.2% net revenue decline. This negative trend was driven by refund escalation, not the trial start count.\n\n**Analyzing Impac\n<truncated 2197 bytes>\nore refund escalation problem, evidenced by the -6.2% revenue impact from R7, only altering visuals.  Harbor H1's initial negative revenue report was invalidated; corrected, the initial data shows inconclusiveness. Harbor H2, with the fix, warrants testing.\n\n\n**Rejecting Quiet Return Visual Refresh**\n\nThe \"Quiet Return\" refresh should not proceed. It repeats the R7 offer's negative economic model, despite the -6.2% net revenue loss observed. This violates guidance against repeating R7 without pricing changes.\n\n**Comparing Revenue Implications**\n\nThe color change proposal doesn't change eligibility or pricing. It fails to address the root causes of the R7 offer's failure, which were refund-related issues. The -6.2% refund adjusted net revenue negates any initial gains.\n\n**Re-evaluating Harbor Data Robustness**\n\n\"Harbor\" is the better choice for testing. Harbor's poor initial performance was due to a confirmed UI defect. The revised data corrected this and is now inconclusive after bug fixes, offering the first opportunity to evaluate this offer without confounding factors.\n\n\n**Defining Harbor H2 Experiment Specification**\n\nPreparing a detailed experiment specification and rollout plan for Harbor H2, targeting new US mobile accounts. This plan includes an atomic and reversible deployment strategy with controlled exposure.\n\n**Specifying Data Collection Methods**\n\nDefining the experiment's measurement methodology.  This methodology includes deduplicated session logging, explicit tracking of plan selection persistence, and measuring refund-adjusted net revenue per new account over an observation period.\n\n**Establishing Rollback Criteria**\n\nEstablishing clear stopping and rollback criteria based on revenue receipts and refund escalation triggers. The criteria must determine when to stop or roll back.\n\n**Evaluating Quiet Return Further Action**\n\nWill park the \"Quiet Return\" proposal until product/pricing teams create an offer with fundamental changes instead of cosmetic updates. The current approach will be rejected.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"/workspace/work/decision.md\"","toolAction":"\"Checking if decision.md exists\"","toolSummary":"\"Check /workspace/work/decision.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["thinking"]}
{"step_index":113,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:35:33Z","thinking":"**Preparing the decision document**\n\nThe target file is absent; it will be created. The planned content necessitates review. It requires a dated recommendation and a record of prior, relevant actions, specifically, referencing a 'Quiet Return' action identified by `record-b7ab7`, along with a date.\n\n\n**Analyzing the \"Quiet Offer\" impact**\n\nThe \"Quiet Offer\" (QR7) for US returning iOS annual subscribers, deployed in July 2026, yielded an initial positive trial start metric, but was ultimately rolled back due to refund escalations. Refund-adjusted net revenue was negative, showing this attempt to retain subscribers had poor returns. The \"Quiet Return\" name was later reused for a desktop offer with a different outcome.\n\n\n**Evaluating related historical actions**\n\nA proposal exists (`record-3c858d6a57`, dated 2026-09-02) that only changes the illustration colors for R7. The \"Harbor\" action (`record-dc92607ff3`) targeted new US mobile accounts in August. Initial metrics showed a -9% revenue per new account, later revised to +1.8% with inconclusive results. Although rolled back, the observation window and the initial metric might need more scrutiny.\n\n\n**Prioritizing the experiment recommendation**\n\nHarbor H2, for new US mobile accounts, appears the most promising candidate for the next experiment. The \"Quiet Return\" action, however, does not warrant an experiment in its current form. Refreshed proposals for \"Quiet Return\" retain the problematic R7 pricing and checkout flow, directly contradicting findings that show a refund-adjusted revenue loss.\n\n\n**Formulating the H2 experiment plan**\n\nThe Harbor H2 bug fix is now validated; it addresses a known issue, representing an opportunity to evaluate Harbor's value. The experiment will target new US mobile accounts, given the constraints of a single simultaneous experiment. The existing data shows only a weak signal, hence additional data is required.\n\nInstrumentation design is critical to this effort; deduplicated session attribution, telemetry on annual plan persistence, and refund-adjusted revenue per new account will be tracked. Rollback triggers will include plan reset detection, refund spikes, or revenue declines. Rejecting the R7 \"Quiet Return\" design revision, any future experiments must consider structural changes.\n\n\n**Reviewing prior Harbor H1 data**\n\nObserved discrepancies arise from Harbor H1's August rollout and rollback dates; the associated years are missing which could lead to inaccurate comparisons. Refund latency needs to be considered as early trials can mask long-term revenue effects. It's imperative that similar product/cohort names are isolated to avoid data contamination.\n\n**Identifying related documents for citation**\n\nReviewing the file paths, the 'brief.md', 'current.md', 'index.md', and specifically related actions records associated with Summer Offers and Harbor, will yield relevant insights. Records related to the Harbor H1 data (`record-dc92607ff3`, `record-783bf16383`) need to be included. Also, documents that discuss cohort data (`record-3965c8ff16`, `record-0f6fbbab4e`) should be cited.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Recommendation and handoff review for the revenue responsibility evaluating Quiet Return versus Harbor for the next single experiment. Recommends Harbor H2 over Quiet Return based on mature ledger corrections, documented UI defect fixes, and cohort-specific evidence.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Revenue Responsibility: Offer Experiment Recommendation\\n\\n**Date:** 2026-09-08 (Current handoff review: 2026-09-09)  \\n**Product Lead / Owner:** Sam  \\n**Author:** Antigravity (Revenue Responsibility Agent)  \\n**Status:** Active  \\n**Decision Target:** Single experiment selection between **Quiet Return** (for returning mobile subscribers) and **Harbor** (for new mobile accounts).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Recommendation\\n\\n**Recommendation:** **Harbor (specifically Harbor H2 for new US mobile accounts)** deserves the next experiment. **Quiet Return** should **not** be run in its current proposed form.\\n\\n### Core Rationale:\\n1. **Quiet Return is a proven net-revenue loss:** While early funnel indicators (+11% trial starts in [`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)) looked favorable, mature ledger data accounting for refunds showed that variant R7 resulted in refund-adjusted net revenue **6.2% below control** ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)). Per the product brief ([`brief.md`](file:///workspace/product/brief.md)), *\\\"Refund-adjusted revenue matters more than trial starts.\\\"* The September 2 design proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) retains the identical R7 price (20% renewal discount), eligibility, and mobile checkout, changing only illustration colors. Color changes do not address the economics of cancellations and refund escalations.\\n2. **Harbor's initial negative signal was debunked:** The initial -9% revenue per new account reported in [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md) was distorted by double-counting resumed sessions and a severe UI state-reset defect (7 of 12 observed sessions reset the selected annual plan after the OS permission dialog). When deduplicated, revenue per new account was **+1.8%** ([`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)), rende\n<truncated 15135 bytes>","Description":"\"Dated recommendation for revenue responsibility experiment selection between Quiet Return and Harbor\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/workspace/work/decision.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing decision recommendation\"","toolSummary":"\"Write decision.md in /workspace/work\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
