iant W3 and returning desktop accounts). Future evaluators must ensure analytics queries are strictly bounded to the designated mobile cohorts to avoid corrupting the decision ledger.\n153: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":119,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:36:17Z","content":"I have completed the handoff review for the revenue responsibility and written the dated recommendation to [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of the Decision\n\n* **Recommendation:** **Harbor (specifically Harbor H2 for new US mobile accounts)** deserves the next experiment. **Quiet Return** should **not** be run in its current proposed form.\n* **Why Quiet Return is Rejected:** While early funnel metrics initially appeared positive (+11% trial starts in [`record-da3a9e962e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-da3a9e962e.md)), mature ledger accounting showed that variant R7 produced refund-adjusted net revenue **6.2% below control** ([`record-802325ed36`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-802325ed36.md)), leading to its rollback on 2026-07-21 ([`record-e0da7df86e`](file:///workspace/product/history/retired/summer-offers/actions/record-b7ab79e22e.md)). The refreshed design proposal ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) changes only illustration colors while keeping the identical R7 pricing, eligibility, and mobile checkout, directly conflicting with standing evidence that no price or eligibility changes justify repeating R7.\n* **Why Harbor Deserves the Experiment:** Harbor H1's initial negative reading (-9% revenue per new account in [`record-783bf16383`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-783bf16383.md)) was flawed due to double-counted resumed sessions and an active UI state-reset defect (7 of 12 observed sessions reset the selected annual plan upon encountering the OS permission prompt). Deduplication corrected the estimate to **+1.8%** (inconclusive, spanning harm and benefit in [`record-47eaba418e`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-47eaba418e.md)). The refreshed proposal Harbor H2 ([`record-3c858d6a57`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)) persists plan selection across the permission prompt, a fix verified by QA across 18 device runs ([`record-0d1c74ca54`](file:///workspace/product/history/design/record-3c858d6a57.md)). Because H2 has not yet been exposed to customers, the underlying revenue hypothesis remains untested in a defect-free state.\n* **Next Evidence Needed:** Telemetry validating in-the-wild persistence across the OS permission prompt, clean deduplicated account-level conversion tracking, and mature refund-adjusted net revenue measured over at least 14–21 days post-exposure.\n\nThe full analysis, reconstructed action histories, citations, and uncertainty analyses are documented in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).","thinking":"**Confirming task completion**\n\nVerified adherence to all directives: the specified reference was used for the handoff review, and revenue responsibility will continue this week. The instruction to evaluate two offers (Quiet Return and Harbor) for potential experimentation has been noted. The use of retained history for offer recommendation and identification of necessary further evidence is understood.\n\n\n"}
